/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  Endothermic dehydrogenation of 2-propanol over a solid catalyst:

      (CH3)2CHOH  ->  (CH3)2CO  +  H2

  NO `dH_rxn` KEY IS WRITTEN HERE, deliberately.  Choupo derives the heat of
  reaction from the species' own formation data (the settled elements datum),
  and that derivation is one of the things this case is here to expose:
  isopropanol's dHf comes from a Joback ESTIMATE, so the reactor duty inherits
  an error from the component record.  Writing Luyben's 62 900 kJ/kmol here
  would override the derivation and hide exactly that.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
dehydrogenation
{
    stoichiometry
    (
        { component isopropanol; nu -1; }
        { component acetone;     nu  1; }
        { component H2;          nu  1; }
    );
    limitingReactant  isopropanol;
}
